    "authorAssociation": "NONE",
    "body": "Hello!\r\n\r\nConsider:\r\n\r\n```md\r\nI'm a markdown file\r\n<!--  ^ cursor here -->\r\n```\r\n\r\n`ysiw[`\r\n\r\nI'd prefer to receive:\r\n\r\n```md\r\nI'm a [markdown] file\r\n```\r\n\r\nBut instead I'll get\r\n\r\n\r\n```md\r\nI'm a [ markdown ] file\r\n```\r\n\r\nAnd same for `(`\r\n\r\nHowever, I might also prefer to pad my square brackets with spaces in JavaScript files\r\n\r\n```js\r\nconst things = 1, 2, 3;\r\n// visual:     _______\r\n```\r\n`S[`\r\n```js\r\nconst things = [ 1, 2, 3 ];\r\n```\r\n\r\nSo, can I configure mini.surround to:\r\n1. pad or not pad, per surround char\r\n2. specify that behaviour per filetype?",
    "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">Hello!</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Consider:</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-text-md notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"I'm a markdown file\n&lt;!--  ^ cursor here --&gt;\"><pre class=\"notranslate\">I'm a markdown file\n<span class=\"pl-c\"><span class=\"pl-c\">&lt;!--</span>  ^ cursor here <span class=\"pl-c\">--&gt;</span></span></pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><code class=\"notranslate\">ysiw[</code></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I'd prefer to receive:</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-text-md notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"I'm a [markdown] file\"><pre class=\"notranslate\">I'm a <span class=\"pl-s\">[</span>markdown<span class=\"pl-s\">]</span> file</pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">But instead I'll get</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-text-md notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"I'm a [ markdown ] file\"><pre class=\"notranslate\">I'm a <span class=\"pl-s\">[</span> markdown <span class=\"pl-s\">]</span> file</pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">And same for <code class=\"notranslate\">(</code></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">However, I might also prefer to pad my square brackets with spaces in JavaScript files</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-js notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"const things = 1, 2, 3;\n// visual:     _______\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><span class=\"pl-k\">const</span> <span class=\"pl-s1\">things</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">1</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">,</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">2</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">,</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">3</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">;</span>\n<span class=\"pl-c\">// visual:     _______</span></pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><code class=\"notranslate\">S[</code></p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-js notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"const things = [ 1, 2, 3 ];\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><span class=\"pl-k\">const</span> <span class=\"pl-s1\">things</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-kos\">[</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">1</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">,</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">2</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">,</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">3</span> <span class=\"pl-kos\">]</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">;</span></pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">So, can I configure mini.surround to:</p>\n<ol dir=\"auto\">\n<li>pad or not pad, per surround char</li>\n<li>specify that behaviour per filetype?</li>\n</ol>",
    "bodyText": "Hello!\nConsider:\nI'm a markdown file\n<!--  ^ cursor here -->\nysiw[\nI'd prefer to receive:\nI'm a [markdown] file\nBut instead I'll get\nI'm a [ markdown ] file\nAnd same for (\nHowever, I might also prefer to pad my square brackets with spaces in JavaScript files\nconst things = 1, 2, 3;\n// visual:     _______\nS[\nconst things = [ 1, 2, 3 ];\nSo, can I configure mini.surround to:\n\npad or not pad, per surround char\nspecify that behaviour per filetype?",
